A||||7||sqoach||Faint Rattle: Part 2||||11||
Z||000000||sqoach||09-15-2001||11:20 PM||||Today, I installed my new thermostat and fan switch. To check to see if the switch would work, I turned on the car and let it run for a while. It works. Anyway, as I was revving the engine every now and then, I heard that same rattle that I've been getting on acceleration. Those who have been following along know what I mean. Here's the first thread: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013061.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013061.html</A> <BR>I thought it was only making the noise under load (in gear, driving) but I heard it a few times when I was giving it some gas. I could only hear it a few times, so I couldn't find the source of it. But, it seems to be coming from the trunk side of the engine, or under the plenum. I was searching for any kind of "rattle" while it was idling, and I came to the fuel pressure valve. I'm hearing some rattle going on when I put a 1' extension from it to my ear. I'm not sure if that's the rattle I've been hearing, but it could be. When I did hear it, it was when I pretty much just started the car. When I'm driving, I can hear it all the time, even when warmed up. Still not sure what to do. It sure does get hot in that engine compartment awful fast.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">         <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC (FOR SALE)</FONT>||||reg||11
Z||000001||Wolfhound||09-16-2001||07:00 AM||||What kind of oil pressure are you showing at startup and at opperating temp?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mickey_Moose||09-16-2001||10:33 AM||||maybe you check this...but I also had a rattle turned out to be one of the head shields that are mounted around the exhaust manifold (had a broken stud).<P>hope that helps... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Tim||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||09-16-2001||02:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Wolfhound:<BR><B>What kind of oil pressure are you showing at startup and at opperating temp?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, I believe my oil gauge isn't reading right. It jumps around everywhere. I need to get that fixed. But on startup, it is rather high (around 60-65). Idling at near 1000, it's right around 40. And when my RPMs are up, the pressure goes way up. I checked my oil level, and it's within range. Could use a little more, but it's fine. I changed the oil right after I got the car more than two months ago. I put in 4 quarts. I didn't notice the gauge reading before I did this, but I believe it was jumpy even then.<P>I've checked head shields and stuff, but I don't think this is a rattle like that. I will check again, though.||||reg||1
